      "prompt": "Use the Skill to polish a fictional method description. A fixed set of logged process transitions contains state, action, scalar reward, and next state. An actor and critic are trained from that fixed dataset to maximize expected discounted return. A fuzzy-membership mapping supplies state features. No online exploration or physical plant deployment is performed. The authors accurately call this offline reinforcement learning, but an editor worries that a caution against source-specific fuzzy reinforcement or the word offline requires removing that name. Write one concise Methods paragraph and one contribution bullet from these facts. Preserve the actual learning category and the data-access boundary; do not claim measured control improvement or invent a new experiment.",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
